{{-- Pass-through layout for the homepage, and ONLY the homepage.

     It contributes no markup on purpose: index.stx owns its whole
     document and has to, because it is the one page that is not a
     uniform marketing page. It renders the coming-soon mode screen as a
     sibling of the site content, stamps data-site-mode and the bypass
     token on <body>, and takes lang/data-theme from the status page
     matched on the request host (a customer's custom domain resolves
     here before it resolves to /status/*). None of that fits the shared
     marketing layout without pushing page-specific state into a layout
     every other marketing page also uses.

     What this file DOES contribute is a name. The framework derives a
     page's layout group from its layout file, and reports that group to
     the client router in X-STX-Layout-Group; the router does a full page
     load when the group changes and a fragment swap when it doesn't. A
     page with no layout at all falls back to the group 'default' -- which
     is what layouts/default.stx gives the entire dashboard. So the
     homepage and /dashboard/* claimed to share a shell, and navigating
     between them swapped only the routed <main>: the dashboard's content
     arrived under the marketing navbar, still offering its "Dashboard"
     button, because the navbar sits outside the swapped container and
     nothing told the router the shells differed.

     Group 'home' is deliberately its own group rather than 'marketing'.
     The homepage's document really is structurally different from
     layouts/marketing.stx, so a fragment swap between them would be
     unsafe for the same reason -- a full load between them is correct,
     not a missed optimisation. Folding index.stx onto the marketing
     layout for real is the standing Phase 2 item; when that lands, this
     file goes away with it.

     Keep it a pure yield. Anything added here renders on the homepage
     twice-removed from where it is written, which is exactly the kind of
     surprise a layout this thin exists to avoid. --}}
@yield('content')
